          zfswatcher - ZFS pool monitoring and notification daemon

                           version history


version 0.6.0 UNRELEASED

 - E-mail notifications use the standard library net/smtp instead of the
   unmaintained github.com/snabb/smtp. STARTTLS is used when the server
   offers it, connections time out after 30 seconds, and the messages now
   carry Message-ID, MIME-Version and UTF-8 headers (non-ASCII subjects are
   encoded). The configuration is unchanged.


version 0.5.0 released 2026-11-21

 - First release of the tantefred fork. Linux (Debian, Proxmox VE) first.

 - Builds with Go modules; the bundled golibs/ directory is gone.

 - Understands current OpenZFS (2.x) output: "0B" sizes, remove:, checkpoint:,
   expand: and condense: sections, scrub and resilver reported together,
   special, dedup, log, cache and spare classes, dRAID, and the file list of
   "zpool status -v".

 - Fixed wrong arguments in the "device state changed" notifications.

 - The Debian package runs the daemon as the unprivileged system user
   "zfswatcher" with a systemd unit (the SysV init script is gone). The
   unit creates /var/log/zfswatcher and hardens the service. The bundled
   zfswatcher-ledctl and its udev rule are installed, so enclosure LEDs work
   without root. If you use ledctl from the ledmon package, add User=root
   with "systemctl edit zfswatcher". Logrotate now rotates
   /var/log/zfswatcher/*.log.

 - The web interface now listens on 127.0.0.1:8081 by default instead of
   all interfaces on port 80, for use behind a reverse proxy. Change "bind"
   in the [www] section to listen elsewhere, for example ":8081" for all
   interfaces. Ports below 1024 need CAP_NET_BIND_SERVICE for the service
   user (see the comment in the systemd unit).

 - The Linux binary is static and built without cgo. It no longer crashes
   with "Illegal instruction" on virtual CPUs without AVX.

 - External commands (zpool, zfs) are killed after 60 seconds, so a hanging
   "zpool status" no longer stops the monitoring.

 - Pools in state SUSPENDED now raise an alert. If you maintain your own
   /etc/zfs/zfswatcher.conf, add SUSPENDED:alert to "poolstatemap" and
   SUSPENDED:text-error to "poolstatecssclassmap"; states missing from these
   maps are treated as severity info.

 - Test suite with real Proxmox VE and Debian 13 fixtures, CI with lint,
   formatting, race detector and vulnerability checks.


version 0.3 released 2013-02-20

 - Disk space usage warnings at configurable thresholds.

 - Experimental FreeBSD and OpenIndiana support.

 - Reconfigure on SIGHUP.

 - Ubuntu ZFS PPA dependency fix.

 - Other minor improvements.


version 0.2 released 2013-02-04

 - Compatibility fix for changes in ZoL 0.6.0-rc14 output formatting.

 - Other minor improvements.


version 0.01 released 2013-02-03

 - Initial release.

